{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1786797072,"nonce":"thqv3+dO50GmNdHE31a0hrYnDSw=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADORPa0Bs8AAAABM4Wu6s8AAAAG3kgryw"},"added":["bug"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1787255040,"nonce":"pAK3t1bs9DvSATgKjkuvHQq9glk=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDORPa0Bs8AAAABP4gHgA","github-url":"https://github.com/FhG-IISB/jNO/issues/101#issuecomment-5360846720"},"message":"Fixed by #116, which merged today.\n\nThe x64 hypothesis in the last bullet was the right one. `tests/test_fem_history_march.py` set `jax_enable_x64` at **module scope**, which runs during collection; any module selected after it that flipped the flag back left this file's Newton march running in float32. That is exactly the observed pattern — passes alone, fails intermittently inside a full run, on a tree that had changed nothing.\n\nForcing float32 on current `main` reproduces the reported failure precisely:\n\n```\nRuntimeError: fem.solve: the load-path march did not converge at step 1 of 4 (tau=0.333333):\nresidual norm nan against the tolerance atol + rtol*||r(u_prev)|| = 8.717e-07\n```\n\nUnder x64 the full file is green — 27 passed, three consecutive runs.\n\n#116 replaced the module-scope flip with the save/restore autouse fixture and added two guards against it coming back: `conftest` restores the flag after every test and warns naming the offender, and a static AST check rejects module-scope writes (which the fixture structurally cannot see, since they happen at import).\n\nWorth recording that the suggested fix is **not** needed here: the tolerance was never the problem. Measuring the residual floor and loosening the gate would have made the test pass while leaving the precision bug in place — and that bug was also behind the unexplained `test_fdm` and `test_bayesian` failure clusters.","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1787255041,"nonce":"5EAjW34sCE2Kbdb9ktNgd02gobk=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADORPa0Bs8AAAABM4Wu6s8AAAAG7iXXEQ"},"status":2}]}